# Normalise line endings per file type.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Some files in this repository are read by programs that only accept one
# line ending. On Windows, Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF
# into CRLF on checkout, which silently breaks them:
#
#   * `backend/crontab` - cron on Linux treats the CR as part of the
#     command, so every job line fails with a syntax error.
#   * `backend/Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml` - tolerated, but the
#     stray CR shows up in build logs and confuses readers.
#
# The rule below marks those files as "must stay LF" regardless of the
# developer's platform.

# --- Files that MUST use LF ---
backend/crontab        text eol=lf
backend/Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml    text eol=lf
*.sh                  text eol=lf
*.yml                 text eol=lf
*.yaml                text eol=lf
*.py                  text eol=lf

# --- Files that are safe to normalise ---
*.md                  text eol=lf
*.ts                  text eol=lf
*.tsx                 text eol=lf
*.json                text eol=lf
*.css                 text eol=lf
*.html                text eol=lf

# --- Binary: never touch ---
*.parquet             binary
*.pkl                 binary
*.joblib              binary
*.pt                  binary
*.npy                 binary
*.png                 binary
*.jpg                 binary
*.ico                 binary
